 of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" 13194139534883 17592186045417 true] [17592186221985 1071 "$x^{′} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x, x_{1}(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{-2t}, x_{2}(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{2t}$\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$, shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" 13194139534883 17592186045417 false] [17592186221985 1074 "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." 13194139534883 17592186045417 true] [17592186221989 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n